          "gallery.modal.1.title": "Computerized Pleoptics",
          "gallery.modal.1.badge": "Pleoptic Therapy",
          "gallery.modal.1.desc": "Interactive software programs ('Crosses', 'Spider', 'Contour') designed to treat amblyopia ('lazy eye') and restore binocular vision. The engaging game-like format makes therapy stress-free for children of all ages.",

          "gallery.modal.2.title": "Autorefractokeratometry",
          "gallery.modal.2.badge": "Computer Diagnostics",
          "gallery.modal.2.desc": "High-precision computer evaluation of ocular refraction and corneal curvature using the Huvitz diagnostic system. Provides instant, non-contact detection of myopia, hyperopia, and astigmatism even in young pediatric patients.",

          "gallery.modal.3.title": "AKA-01 Apparatus (Accommodation Assessment #1)",
          "gallery.modal.3.badge": "Accommodation Diagnostics",
          "gallery.modal.3.desc": "Automated AKA-01 diagnostic complex for objective evaluation of absolute and relative accommodation reserves. Measures ciliary muscle stamina and detects focal spasm caused by intense screen or reading fatigue.",

          "gallery.modal.4.title": "Ocular Vibromassage (Gezatone)",
          "gallery.modal.4.badge": "Physiotherapy & Relaxation",
          "gallery.modal.4.desc": "Delicate pneumatic and vibrational massage of the periorbital area using Gezatone therapeutic goggles with gentle infrared warming. Relieves accommodation spasm, eliminates digital eye strain, and enhances microcirculation.",

          "gallery.modal.5.title": "AKA-01 Apparatus (Accommodation Dynamics #2)",
          "gallery.modal.5.badge": "Treatment Monitoring",
          "gallery.modal.5.desc": "Assessment of dynamic focal characteristics and ciliary muscle endurance during device-based therapy. Enables the attending specialist to monitor individual treatment progress with high accuracy.",

          "gallery.modal.6.title": "Rucheyok Accommodation Trainer",
          "gallery.modal.6.badge": "Device-Based Training",
          "gallery.modal.6.desc": "Specialized ophthalmic trainer designed to stimulate visual accommodation. Light stimuli sequentially shift across varying distances, exercising the ciliary muscle to improve focal reserves and slow myopia progression.",

          "gallery.modal.7.title": "Synoptophore",
          "gallery.modal.7.badge": "Orthoptic Strabismus Therapy",
          "gallery.modal.7.desc": "The primary orthoptic instrument for strabismus evaluation and treatment, developing binocular and stereoscopic vision. Separates visual fields for each eye, training the brain to merge dual images into a unified 3D perception.",

          "gallery.modal.8.title": "Macular Laser Stimulation ('Speckle-M')",
          "gallery.modal.8.badge": "Laser-Optical Stimulation",
          "gallery.modal.8.desc": "Laser and LED stimulation of the central macular retina using a dynamic red speckle pattern. Highly effective for amblyopia of various etiologies, retinal dystrophies, and optic nerve fatigue.",

          "gallery.modal.9.title": "Anterior Segment Examination",
          "gallery.modal.9.badge": "Primary Focal Exam",
          "gallery.modal.9.desc": "Detailed focal examination of the cornea, conjunctiva, iris, and crystalline lens using focused side lighting. Enables the ophthalmologist to detect micro-trauma, inflammatory signs, and structural anomalies.",

          "gallery.modal.10.title": "Biomicroscopy (Slit Lamp)",
          "gallery.modal.10.badge": "Microscopic Diagnostics",
          "gallery.modal.10.desc": "Non-contact examination of optical media and deep ocular structures under high magnification using a slit lamp stereomicroscope. Allows meticulous assessment of the cornea, anterior chamber, lens, and vitreous.",

          "gallery.modal.11.title": "AMO-ATOS + AMBLIO-1",
          "gallery.modal.11.badge": "Magnetotherapy & Photostimulation",
          "gallery.modal.11.desc": "Combined magnetotherapy with photostimulation. A running magnetic field paired with the 'AMBLIO-1' light-pulse attachment provides vasodilating, spasmolytic, and anti-edema action, enhancing tissue nutrition in accommodation spasm and amblyopia.",


